50,3,1,talk,Servas,,"The candidates are A: Clinic Scheduler, B: Harvest Sensor, C: Fabric Loop, and D: Ledger Bridge. I lean toward D.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Asuka,,D fits the profile of our successful exits and avoids the retention issues I saw in shopkeeper tools.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Minako,,"D is software-based, which helps with our credit line issues and avoids the physical asset drain.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Mio,,"D doesn't need seasonal crews or warehouse supervisors, which makes my hiring concerns disappear!","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"A has security delays, B and C have hardware/logistics risks. D is the most efficient path to deployment.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Servas,,It seems we are in rare agreement. D offers the cleanest reporting and lowest operational friction.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Asuka,,I agree. The risk profile of C is too high given the write-off history.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Minako,,And B's hardware would likely trigger the appraisal fees Servas mentioned.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Mio,,D is definitely the way to go!,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Toshio,,I concur.,"{""words"":2,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
